is and Glasgow both come up as top cities for me. <br /> <br /> However I grew up in the Pacific Northwest and so learned about Seattle and how it was taken/stolen, then built, then built on top of, the various sociological reforms, etc. Did you know it was the last city on the way to the Klondike/Alaskan gold rush? Did you know 'Shanghai-ing' was a huge issue in Seattle Saloons? Did you know there is a whole under city that the modern city is built on top of? With the art and music movements of the 60s and 70s there is a deep passionate history and in modern days there is a lot of emotion about conservation combined with humane assistance. It could be a fascinating US City book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1559-cryocube","name":"cryocube","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T18:24:41-08:00","id":55090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cryocube</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/47844-wraith-which-cities-would-you-like-to-see-as-necropoli?p=54040#post54040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Paris and Glasgow both come up as top cities for me.<br /> <br /> However I grew up in the Pacific Northwest and so learned about Seattle and how it was taken/stolen, then built, then built on top of, the various sociological reforms, etc. Did you know it was the last city on the way to the Klondike/Alaskan gold rush? Did you know 'Shanghai-ing' was a huge issue in Seattle Saloons? Did you know there is a whole under city that the modern city is built on top of? With the art and music movements of the 60s and 70s there is a deep passionate history and in modern days there is a lot of emotion about conservation combined with humane assistance. It could be a fascinating US City book.</div> </div> </div> </div>First person to ask me about Kurt Cobain gets fed to a Malfean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T20:42:51-08:00","id":55181,"title":"","content":"There's so many good suggestions by so many people who seem to know the ins. outs and sideways of their particular town, I imagine if there was a framework to fill out, people could make their own Necropoli books and share them. Unless eventually OPP wants to create The Big Book of Necropoli Companion book for Wraith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T23:18:43-08:00","id":55275,"title":"","content":"If your doing battlefields then I'm chipping in Wilson's Creek.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T10:37:58-08:00","id":55546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RealDeadguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/47844-wraith-which-cities-would-you-like-to-see-as-necropoli?p=55090#post55090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> First person to ask me about Kurt Cobain gets fed to a Malfean.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like Kurt Cobain IS a Malfean","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1559-cryocube","name":"cryocube","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T10:44:53-08:00","id":55550,"title":"","content":"I've got a whole bunch of notes from the decade we spent living and gaming in El Paso, Texas. I have them in a huge binder labeled &quot;El Paso by Night&quot; even though by the end of ten years, it was turning out to be more &quot;the American Southwest by Night Chronicles.&quot; And while I'd love to see El Paso mentioned more in materials, what I'd really like to see is the Necropoli of someplace like Cuidad Juarez. It might just be one huge, gaping nihil, with the Legionnaires standing on a soulsteel bulwark wall, which is a reflection the fence between El Paso and Juarez, hunkered down against the storm and the fury of the Tempest pouring out of this wound in reality...<br /> <br /> Well, shit. I just gave myself an idea.<br /> <br /> (For those of you not familiar with it, Cuidad Juarez in Chihuahua, Mexico was once labeled &quot;the murder capitol of the world.&quot; Downtown Juarez is a twenty minute walk over a bridge from downtown El Paso. They are basically one city, with about 3 million people. Ironically, laughably, El Paso was just awarded the &quot;Safest City in America&quot; award for the fourth year in a row. [This is because they only consider within the city limits. There is a shitload of desert to bury the bodies. Oh, yeah, and <i>THE MURDER CAPITOL OF THE WORLD</i> is just a leisurely stroll away.] Oh, and to make matters more fucked-up, close to 400 women have been murdered and left to rot in the desert since 1993. And for anybody that thinks it's so far away, that it could never happen so close to America, one can see the entirety of Juarez from Scenic Drive, the pass that wraps around the mountain, and I would also like to point out that people in Juarez build their houses <i>right up against</i> the chainlink fence seperating America and Mexico. But when you live there, it's just a part of life.)<br /> <br /> Cheers (I guess. I've made myself sad/angry now).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T16:59:22-08:00","id":55811,"title":"","content":"ok.... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Necropolis Rome<br /> also know as &quot;Stygia above the Tempest&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" marg